PROJECT: Cerebro — AI-Adaptive Board Exam Prep Platform
STACK: Next.js 16 (App Router, Turbopack), TypeScript strict, Supabase, Tailwind CSS 4, shadcn/ui
DESIGN: Rams Standard — Braun-inspired minimal aesthetic. Achromatic palette (warm whites, greys, charcoal) with functional amber/green/red accents. No gradients, no shadows heavier than 0 1px 3px rgba(26,26,26,0.06). Transitions at 150ms ease.

PAYMENTS: PayRex (primary, PH — GCash/Maya/Card/QR Ph) + Stripe (international fallback). Use lib/payments/provider.ts abstraction.

ADMIN: Users with is_admin=true on profiles table get Max-tier access by default. Admin can spoof tiers via Developer Settings (/dashboard/settings/developer). Use getAdminAwareProfile() and hasTierAccess() for all tier checks.

RULES:
1. Server Components by default. Only add 'use client' when useState/useEffect/event handlers are needed.
2. Server Actions for all database mutations. Never expose Supabase writes client-side.
3. Use @supabase/ssr for auth. NEVER use localStorage for auth state.
4. No useEffect for data fetching. Use RSC async or the use() hook.
5. RLS is enabled on ALL tables. Check policies before adding features.
6. TypeScript strict mode. No 'any'. Use Supabase-generated types.
7. Tailwind only for styling. No inline styles. No CSS modules.
8. shadcn/ui for base components. Customize colors via CSS variables.
9. Lucide icons only. Stroke 1.5px, 20px default size.
10. Mobile-first responsive design. Touch targets min 44px.
11. For tier gates: always use getAdminAwareProfile() + hasTierAccess(), never raw profile.tier checks.

DATABASE: See PRD.md Section 6 + migration 002 for is_admin and payrex columns.

DEMO MODE: When NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is empty, app runs in demo mode with mock data. See lib/demo/ for mock Supabase client and data. Dashboard routes are at /dashboard/* (not a route group).

QUIZ UI: Single column, max-width 720px, centered. Full-screen immersive. Optimistic UI for answers.

ROUTING: Dashboard pages are under src/app/dashboard/ (real route segment, not a route group). Auth pages are under src/app/(auth)/ (route group). Never pass React component functions from Server Components to Client Components — pass string identifiers and resolve on the client side.
